 "final_text": "The proof is in `/work/putnam_2007_b5.lean`. `lean /work/putnam_2007_b5.lean` now exits 0 with no errors, no `sorry` warning, and no axioms. The docstring, imports, and theorem statement are unchanged.\n\nThe argument: let m = \u230an/k\u230b and r = n \u2212 km, so 0 \u2264 r < k. Define F(X) = \u220f_{j<k} (n \u2212 kX \u2212 j) as a polynomial in X with coefficients in \u211d[n]. F vanishes at X = m because one factor is zero. Its X^k coefficient is the constant (\u2212k)^k, so solving for m^k gives P_i(n) = \u2212F_i(n)/(\u2212k)^k.\n\nThe file has one cosmetic quirk: the splice leaves `:=` followed by `by` on its own line at column 0, which Lean accepts.",
